 "root_cause": "Missing or falsey ASR segment times became zero anchors. Invalid temporal order or duration was only rejected by the host after inference, allowing further segment consumption and partial worker output before detection.",
 "changes": [
  "Validate each nonempty segment start/end before retention; reject absent, null, boolean, textual, nonfinite, negative, excessive-duration and overflowing times",
  "Enforce start <= end and the host 1ms ordering tolerance while consuming segments",
  "Stop at the first unusable segment, close its iterator and never write a partial transcript or trigger an extra non-VAD retry",
  "Preserve real zero, the 7200-second boundary, blank-segment skipping and fallback only for empty VAD output",
  "Keep existing inference/conversion failure identity and cleanup context behavior; known unusable transcripts leave a reusable worker"
 ],
